{"name":"Cartoon Violence","hex":"#d01722","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cartoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A humorous drawing, often with a caption, or a strip of such drawings.","A drawing satirising current public figures."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw a cartoon, a humorous drawing.","To make a preliminary sketch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cartoon"},{"term":"violence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Extreme force.","Physical action which causes destruction, harm, pain, or suffering."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To subject to violence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cartoon violence","blocks":[{"text":"Cartoon violence is the representation of violent actions involving animated characters and situations. This may include violence where a character is unharmed after the action has been inflicted. Animated violence is sometimes partitioned into comedic and non-comedic cartoon violence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png/330px-Dover_boys_triple_knockout.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartoon_violence","wikidata":"Q4684044"},{"title":"Cartoon Violence (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cartoon Violence is the second studio album indie rock band Herzog, released on March 19, 2012 on Exit Stencil Recordings. It was recorded more collaboratively than their debut album, Search, with Nick Tolar assisted by Tony Vorell, who wrote the album's lyrics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b3/Cartoon_Violence_Herzog_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartoon_Violence_(album)","wikidata":"Q16245288"},{"title":"Cartoon","blocks":[{"text":"A cartoon is a type of visual art that is typically drawn, frequently animated, in an unrealistic or semi-realistic style. The specific meaning has evolved, but the modern usage usually refers to either: an image or series of images intended for satire, caricature, or humor; or a motion picture that relies on a sequence of illustrations for its animation. Someone who creates cartoons in the first sense is called a cartoonist, and in the second sense they are usually called an animator."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/SubstanceandShadow.jpg/330px-SubstanceandShadow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cartoon","wikidata":"Q627603"},{"title":"Violence","blocks":[{"text":"Violence is characterized as the use of physical force by humans to cause harm to other living beings, such as pain, injury, disablement, death, damage and destruction. The World Health Organization (WHO) defines violence as \"the intentional use of physical force or power, threatened or actual, against oneself, another person, or against a group or community, which either results in or has a high likelihood of resulting in injury, death, psychological harm, maldevelopment, or deprivation\"; it recognizes the need to include violence not resulting in injury or death."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violence","wikidata":"Q124490"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/V%26A_-_Raphael%2C_Christ%27s_Charge_to_Peter_%281515%29.jpg/500px-V%26A_-_Raphael%2C_Christ%27s_Charge_to_Peter_%281515%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/V%26A_-_Raphael%2C_Christ%27s_Charge_to_Peter_%281515%29.jpg/500px-V%26A_-_Raphael%2C_Christ%27s_Charge_to_Peter_%281515%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christ's Charge to Peter, one of the Raphael Cartoons, 